> On Friday, February 8, 2013 5:26:19 PM UTC+3, .asiz. wrote:
>>
>> What is exactly the problem with {mi cortu lo bekpi}?
>>
>
> that bekpi2 is not filled.
>

Yes it is. Context is everything. Since {lo bekpi} is {lo se cortu}, it
must be {lo berti be lo cortu}.

The only way it could be a back belonging to an individual /other/ than {lo
cortu} is if that individual is an empath, and even then it wouldn't be
{ko'a cortu lo bekpi be ko'e}, but {ko'a lifri lonu ko'e cortu lo bekpi}.


